IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-persons`
IMPORT `uc3-sch4-payments`

-- The Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Schedule 2 (claimant treated as liable or not liable to make payments).
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt (plain-text rendering, not the official text). Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Layer 1.
--
-- WHAT THIS SCHEDULE DECIDES. Regulation 25(5) asks whether the claimant is liable to make the payments. This Schedule widens that (Part 1:
-- the claimant is treated as liable although someone else is) and narrows it (Part 2: the claimant is treated as not liable although they are).
-- The Schedule never says which Part prevails if both apply to the same liability. The composite rule at the end reads Part 2 as prevailing
-- (fork U3-F15, assumed and not ruled): every Part 2 provision is written as an exception, and paragraphs 9(2) and 10(2) show the draftsman
-- thinking of Part 2 as a set of overrides.
--
-- OUT OF RANGE, taken as facts: regulation 3(4) (claiming as a single person), regulation 4 ("responsible for a child"). "Close relative" and
-- "claim basis" are the keel's. Whether the Secretary of State is satisfied (paragraph 10) is a stated input, as are the judgements in paragraph 2.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Which kind of payment a liability is for.
-- src:1971 | (1) Where the arrangements under which the claimant occupies the accommodation provide for rent free periods, the claimant is to be treated as liable to make rent payments and service charge payments in respect of accommodation for the whole of any rent free period.
@ref Sch 2 para 4(1) (src:1971)
DECLARE `Kind of payment under Schedule 2` IS ONE OF
    `rent payments`
    `service charge payments`
    `owner-occupier payments`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Part 1, paragraph 1: the person who is liable is a child or qualifying young person the claimant is responsible for, or (for a member of a
-- couple claiming as a single person) the other member of the couple, unless the claimant is a single person by virtue of regulation 3(4).
-- src:1954 | (1) A claimant is to be treated as liable to make payments where the person who is liable to make the payments is—
-- src:1955 | (a) any child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant (or if the claimant is a member of a couple, either member) is responsible; or
-- src:1956 | (b) in the case of a claimant who is a member of a couple claiming as a single person, the other member of the couple.
-- src:1957 | (2) Sub-paragraph (1)(b) does not apply to a person who is claiming as a single person by virtue of regulation 3(4).
@ref Sch 2 para 1 (src:1954-1957)
DECLARE `Person who is liable to make the payments` HAS
    -- out of range: reg 4 (piece uc1), "responsible for a child or qualifying young person"
    `a child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant (or if the claimant is a member of a couple, either member) is responsible`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other member of the couple of which the claimant is a member`                                                                IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1954 | (1) A claimant is to be treated as liable to make payments where the person who is liable to make the payments is—
-- src:1955 | (a) any child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant (or if the claimant is a member of a couple, either member) is responsible; or
-- src:1956 | (b) in the case of a claimant who is a member of a couple claiming as a single person, the other member of the couple.
-- src:1957 | (2) Sub-paragraph (1)(b) does not apply to a person who is claiming as a single person by virtue of regulation 3(4).
@ref Sch 2 para 1 (src:1954-1957)
GIVEN person IS A `Person who is liable to make the payments`
      basis IS A `Claim basis`
      `claiming as a single person by virtue of regulation 3(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 1 — the claimant is treated as liable because of the person who is liable` person basis `claiming as a single person by virtue of regulation 3(4)` MEANS
    (person's `a child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant (or if the claimant is a member of a couple, either member) is responsible`)
    OR (    (person's `the other member of the couple of which the claimant is a member`)
        AND (basis EQUALS `a single claimant who is a member of a couple`)
        AND (NOT `claiming as a single person by virtue of regulation 3(4)`))

-- Part 1, paragraph 2: failure to pay by the person who is liable. The judgements in (c) and (d) are stated inputs.
-- Sub-paragraph (3), for owner-occupier payments, says only what regard may be had to when deciding (d): it is carried in the description of that input.
-- src:1959 | (1) A claimant is to be treated as liable to make payments where all of the conditions specified in sub-paragraph (2) are met.
-- src:1960 | (2) These are the conditions—
-- src:1961 | (a) the person who is liable to make the payments is not doing so;
-- src:1962 | (b) the claimant has to make the payments in order to continue occupation of the accommodation;
-- src:1963 | (c) the claimant's circumstances are such that it would be unreasonable to expect them to make other arrangements;
-- src:1964 | (d) it is otherwise reasonable in all the circumstances to treat the claimant as liable to make the payments.
-- src:1965 | (3) In determining what is reasonable for the purposes of sub-paragraph (2)(d) in the case of owner-occupier payments, regard may be had to the fact that continuing to make the payments may benefit the person with the liability to make the payments.
@ref Sch 2 para 2 (src:1959-1965)
DECLARE `Failure to pay by the person who is liable` HAS
    `the person who is liable to make the payments is not doing so`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant has to make the payments in order to continue occupation of the accommodation`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant's circumstances are such that it would be unreasonable to expect them to make other arrangements`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is otherwise reasonable in all the circumstances to treat the claimant as liable to make the payments`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1959 | (1) A claimant is to be treated as liable to make payments where all of the conditions specified in sub-paragraph (2) are met.
-- src:1960 | (2) These are the conditions—
-- src:1961 | (a) the person who is liable to make the payments is not doing so;
-- src:1962 | (b) the claimant has to make the payments in order to continue occupation of the accommodation;
-- src:1963 | (c) the claimant's circumstances are such that it would be unreasonable to expect them to make other arrangements;
-- src:1964 | (d) it is otherwise reasonable in all the circumstances to treat the claimant as liable to make the payments.
@ref Sch 2 para 2(1) and (2) (src:1959-1964)
GIVEN failure IS A `Failure to pay by the person who is liable`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 2 — the claimant is treated as liable because the person who is liable has failed to pay` failure MEANS
    (failure's `the person who is liable to make the payments is not doing so`)
    AND (failure's `the claimant has to make the payments in order to continue occupation of the accommodation`)
    AND (failure's `the claimant's circumstances are such that it would be unreasonable to expect them to make other arrangements`)
    AND (failure's `it is otherwise reasonable in all the circumstances to treat the claimant as liable to make the payments`)

-- Part 1, paragraph 3: liability waived in return for repair work.
-- src:1967 | A claimant is to be treated as liable to make payments where—
-- src:1968 | (a) the liability to make payments is waived by the person (“P”) to whom the liability is owed; and
-- src:1969 | (b) the waiver of that liability is by way of reasonable compensation for reasonable repair or re-decoration works carried out by the claimant to the accommodation which P would otherwise have carried out or been required to carry out.
@ref Sch 2 para 3 (src:1967-1969)
DECLARE `Waiver of liability for repair work` HAS
    `the liability to make payments is waived by the person to whom the liability is owed`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the waiver is by way of reasonable compensation for reasonable repair or re-decoration works carried out by the claimant to the accommodation`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the works are works which the person to whom the liability is owed would otherwise have carried out or been required to carry out`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1967 | A claimant is to be treated as liable to make payments where—
-- src:1968 | (a) the liability to make payments is waived by the person (“P”) to whom the liability is owed; and
-- src:1969 | (b) the waiver of that liability is by way of reasonable compensation for reasonable repair or re-decoration works carried out by the claimant to the accommodation which P would otherwise have carried out or been required to carry out.
@ref Sch 2 para 3 (src:1967-1969)
GIVEN waiver IS A `Waiver of liability for repair work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 3 — the claimant is treated as liable although the liability is waived for repair work` waiver MEANS
    (waiver's `the liability to make payments is waived by the person to whom the liability is owed`)
    AND (waiver's `the waiver is by way of reasonable compensation for reasonable repair or re-decoration works carried out by the claimant to the accommodation`)
    AND (waiver's `the works are works which the person to whom the liability is owed would otherwise have carried out or been required to carry out`)

-- Part 1, paragraph 4: for the whole of any rent free period, the claimant is treated as liable for rent payments and service charge payments.
-- "Rent free period" is Schedule 4 paragraph 7(4): `Sch 4 para 7(4) — a rent free period`.
-- src:1971 | (1) Where the arrangements under which the claimant occupies the accommodation provide for rent free periods, the claimant is to be treated as liable to make rent payments and service charge payments in respect of accommodation for the whole of any rent free period.
-- src:1972 | (2) In paragraph (1), “rent free period” has the meaning given in paragraph 7(4) of Schedule 4.
@ref Sch 2 para 4 (src:1971-1972)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of payment under Schedule 2`
      `the arrangements provide for rent free periods` IS A BOOLEAN
      period IS A `Period of the arrangements`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 4 — the claimant is treated as liable for the whole of a rent free period` kind `the arrangements provide for rent free periods` period MEANS
    `the arrangements provide for rent free periods`
    AND (    (kind EQUALS `rent payments`)
          OR (kind EQUALS `service charge payments`))
    AND (`Sch 4 para 7(4) — a rent free period` period)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Part 2, paragraph 5: liability to a person who lives in the accommodation and is the other member of the couple, a child or qualifying young
-- person the claimant (or the other member) is responsible for, or a close relative of the claimant, the other member or such a child.
-- src:1974 | 5 Liability to make rent and other payments to close relative
-- src:1975 | (1) A claimant is to be treated as not liable to make rent payments where the liability to make them is owed to a person who lives in the accommodation and who is—
-- src:1976 | (a) if the claimant is a member of a couple, the other member; or
-- src:1977 | (b) a child or qualifying young person for whom—
-- src:1978 | (i) the claimant is responsible, or
-- src:1979 | (ii) if the claimant is a member of a couple, the other member is responsible; or
-- src:1980 | (c) a close relative of—
-- src:1981 | (i) the claimant, or
-- src:1982 | (ii) if the claimant is a member of a couple, the other member, or
-- src:1983 | (iii) any child or qualifying young person who falls within paragraph (b).
@ref Sch 2 para 5(1) (src:1974-1983)
DECLARE `Person to whom a liability is owed` HAS
    `the person lives in the accommodation`                                                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other member of the couple of which the claimant is a member`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    -- out of range: reg 4 (piece uc1), "responsible for a child or qualifying young person"
    `a child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant (or if the claimant is a member of a couple, the other member) is responsible`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person as a possible close relative of the claimant`                                                       IS A `Possible close relative`
    `the person as a possible close relative of the other member of the couple`                                     IS A `Possible close relative`
    `the person as a possible close relative of a child or qualifying young person who falls within paragraph (b)`  IS A `Possible close relative`

-- src:1975 | (1) A claimant is to be treated as not liable to make rent payments where the liability to make them is owed to a person who lives in the accommodation and who is—
-- src:1976 | (a) if the claimant is a member of a couple, the other member; or
-- src:1977 | (b) a child or qualifying young person for whom—
-- src:1978 | (i) the claimant is responsible, or
-- src:1979 | (ii) if the claimant is a member of a couple, the other member is responsible; or
-- src:1980 | (c) a close relative of—
-- src:1981 | (i) the claimant, or
-- src:1982 | (ii) if the claimant is a member of a couple, the other member, or
-- src:1983 | (iii) any child or qualifying young person who falls within paragraph (b).
@ref Sch 2 para 5(1) (src:1975-1983)
GIVEN creditor IS A `Person to whom a liability is owed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 5(1) — the liability is owed to a person who lives in the accommodation and is within paragraph 5(1)(a) to (c)` creditor MEANS
    (creditor's `the person lives in the accommodation`)
    AND (    (creditor's `the other member of the couple of which the claimant is a member`)
          OR (creditor's `a child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant (or if the claimant is a member of a couple, the other member) is responsible`)
          OR (`reg 2 — close relative` (creditor's `the person as a possible close relative of the claimant`))
          OR (`reg 2 — close relative` (creditor's `the person as a possible close relative of the other member of the couple`))
          OR (`reg 2 — close relative` (creditor's `the person as a possible close relative of a child or qualifying young person who falls within paragraph (b)`)))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Part 2, paragraph 6(5) and (6): a person's associates, and the holdings of the person and the associates "taken together".
-- src:2008 | (6) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (5), “associate”, in relation to a person (“A”) holding shares in an undertaking (“X”) or entitled to exercise or control the exercise of voting power in relation to another undertaking (“Y”), means—
-- src:2009 | (a) the spouse or civil partner of A;
-- src:2010 | (b) a child or step-child of A (if under 18);
-- src:2011 | (c) the trustee of any settlement under which A has a life interest in possession (in Scotland a life interest);
-- src:2012 | (d) an undertaking of which A is a director;
-- src:2013 | (e) a person who is an employee or partner of A;
-- src:2014 | (f) if A has with any other person an agreement or arrangement with respect to the acquisition, holding or disposal of shares or other interests in X or Y, that other person;
-- src:2015 | (g) if A has with any other person an agreement or arrangement under which they undertake to act together in exercising their voting power in relation to X or Y, that other person.
@ref Sch 2 para 6(6) (src:2008-2015)
DECLARE `Person who may be an associate` HAS
    `spouse or civil partner of A`                                                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `child or step-child of A`                                                                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `age in complete years`                                                                                          IS A NUMBER
    `trustee of a settlement under which A has a life interest in possession (in Scotland a life interest)`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `undertaking of which A is a director`                                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `employee or partner of A`                                                                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `has with A an agreement or arrangement with respect to the acquisition, holding or disposal of shares or other interests in X or Y`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `has with A an agreement or arrangement under which they undertake to act together in exercising their voting power in relation to X or Y`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2009 | (a) the spouse or civil partner of A;
-- src:2010 | (b) a child or step-child of A (if under 18);
-- src:2011 | (c) the trustee of any settlement under which A has a life interest in possession (in Scotland a life interest);
-- src:2012 | (d) an undertaking of which A is a director;
-- src:2013 | (e) a person who is an employee or partner of A;
-- src:2014 | (f) if A has with any other person an agreement or arrangement with respect to the acquisition, holding or disposal of shares or other interests in X or Y, that other person;
-- src:2015 | (g) if A has with any other person an agreement or arrangement under which they undertake to act together in exercising their voting power in relation to X or Y, that other person.
@ref Sch 2 para 6(6) (src:2009-2015)
GIVEN person IS A `Person who may be an associate`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 6(6) — associate` person MEANS
    (person's `spouse or civil partner of A`)
    OR ((person's `child or step-child of A`) AND (person's `age in complete years` LESS THAN 18))
    OR (person's `trustee of a settlement under which A has a life interest in possession (in Scotland a life interest)`)
    OR (person's `undertaking of which A is a director`)
    OR (person's `employee or partner of A`)
    OR (person's `has with A an agreement or arrangement with respect to the acquisition, holding or disposal of shares or other interests in X or Y`)
    OR (person's `has with A an agreement or arrangement under which they undertake to act together in exercising their voting power in relation to X or Y`)

-- A holder: the person (A) or an associate, with the holdings that paragraph 6(4)(a) to (h) measures. Percentages are of "shares" and
-- "voting power" as paragraph 6(8) defines them (fork U3-F17: the definitions fix what is measured, and the percentages are stated inputs).
-- src:1995 | (4) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (3), A has a material interest in C if A—
-- src:1996 | (a) holds at least 10% of the shares in C; or
-- src:1997 | (b) is able to exercise a significant influence over the management of C by virtue of A's shareholding in C; or
-- src:1998 | (c) holds at least 10% of the shares in a parent undertaking (“P”) of C; or
-- src:1999 | (d) is able to exercise a significant influence over the management of P by virtue of A's shareholding in P; or
-- src:2000 | (e) is entitled to exercise, or control the exercise of, voting power in C which, if it consists of voting rights, constitutes at least 10% of the voting rights in C; or
-- src:2001 | (f) is able to exercise a significant influence over the management of C by virtue of A's entitlement to exercise, or control the exercise of, voting rights in C; or
-- src:2002 | (g) is entitled to exercise, or control the exercise of, voting power in P which, if it consists of voting rights, constitutes at least 10% of the voting rights in P; or
-- src:2003 | (h) is able to exercise a significant influence over the management of P by virtue of A's entitlement to exercise, or control the exercise of, voting rights in P.
@ref Sch 2 para 6(4) (src:1995-2003)
DECLARE `Holder of an interest in a company` HAS
    `the holder is the person (A)`                                                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the holder as a possible associate of the person`                                                                      IS A `Person who may be an associate`
    `percentage of the shares in C held`                                                                                    IS A NUMBER
    `able to exercise a significant influence over the management of C by virtue of the holder's shareholding in C`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `percentage of the shares in a parent undertaking (P) of C held`                                                        IS A NUMBER
    `able to exercise a significant influence over the management of P by virtue of the holder's shareholding in P`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `percentage of the voting rights in C that the holder is entitled to exercise, or control the exercise of`              IS A NUMBER
    `able to exercise a significant influence over the management of C by virtue of the holder's entitlement to exercise, or control the exercise of, voting rights in C`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `percentage of the voting rights in P that the holder is entitled to exercise, or control the exercise of`              IS A NUMBER
    `able to exercise a significant influence over the management of P by virtue of the holder's entitlement to exercise, or control the exercise of, voting rights in P`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2004 | (5) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (4), references to “A” are to—
-- src:2005 | (a) the person; or
-- src:2006 | (b) any of the person's associates; or
-- src:2007 | (c) the person and any of the person's associates taken together.
@ref Sch 2 para 6(5) (src:2004-2007)
GIVEN holder IS A `Holder of an interest in a company`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 6(5) — the holder counts as A or one of A's associates` holder MEANS
    (holder's `the holder is the person (A)`)
    OR (`Sch 2 para 6(6) — associate` (holder's `the holder as a possible associate of the person`))

-- The holdings of the person and the person's associates taken together (paragraph 6(5)(c)). Because paragraph 6(5)(a) and (b) test the person
-- alone, or any one associate alone, and every limb of paragraph 6(4) is monotone in the holding (a larger holding, or one more holder with
-- influence, never loses an interest), the combined holding satisfies a limb whenever either of those does. Only the combined holding is computed.
-- src:2004 | (5) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (4), references to “A” are to—
-- src:2005 | (a) the person; or
-- src:2006 | (b) any of the person's associates; or
-- src:2007 | (c) the person and any of the person's associates taken together.
@ref Sch 2 para 6(5) (src:2004-2007)
GIVEN holders IS A LIST OF `Holder of an interest in a company`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 2 para 6(5)(c) — the percentage of the shares in C held by the person and the associates together` holders MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN holder YIELD IF `Sch 2 para 6(5) — the holder counts as A or one of A's associates` holder THEN holder's `percentage of the shares in C held` ELSE 0) holders)

-- src:2004 | (5) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (4), references to “A” are to—
-- src:2005 | (a) the person; or
-- src:2006 | (b) any of the person's associates; or
-- src:2007 | (c) the person and any of the person's associates taken together.
@ref Sch 2 para 6(5) (src:2004-2007)
GIVEN holders IS A LIST OF `Holder of an interest in a company`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 2 para 6(5)(c) — the percentage of the shares in P held by the person and the associates together` holders MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN holder YIELD IF `Sch 2 para 6(5) — the holder counts as A or one of A's associates` holder THEN holder's `percentage of the shares in a parent undertaking (P) of C held` ELSE 0) holders)

-- src:2004 | (5) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (4), references to “A” are to—
-- src:2005 | (a) the person; or
-- src:2006 | (b) any of the person's associates; or
-- src:2007 | (c) the person and any of the person's associates taken together.
@ref Sch 2 para 6(5) (src:2004-2007)
GIVEN holders IS A LIST OF `Holder of an interest in a company`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 2 para 6(5)(c) — the percentage of the voting rights in C held by the person and the associates together` holders MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN holder YIELD IF `Sch 2 para 6(5) — the holder counts as A or one of A's associates` holder THEN holder's `percentage of the voting rights in C that the holder is entitled to exercise, or control the exercise of` ELSE 0) holders)

-- src:2004 | (5) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (4), references to “A” are to—
-- src:2005 | (a) the person; or
-- src:2006 | (b) any of the person's associates; or
-- src:2007 | (c) the person and any of the person's associates taken together.
@ref Sch 2 para 6(5) (src:2004-2007)
GIVEN holders IS A LIST OF `Holder of an interest in a company`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 2 para 6(5)(c) — the percentage of the voting rights in P held by the person and the associates together` holders MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN holder YIELD IF `Sch 2 para 6(5) — the holder counts as A or one of A's associates` holder THEN holder's `percentage of the voting rights in P that the holder is entitled to exercise, or control the exercise of` ELSE 0) holders)

-- src:1995 | (4) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (3), A has a material interest in C if A—
-- src:1996 | (a) holds at least 10% of the shares in C; or
-- src:1997 | (b) is able to exercise a significant influence over the management of C by virtue of A's shareholding in C; or
-- src:1998 | (c) holds at least 10% of the shares in a parent undertaking (“P”) of C; or
-- src:1999 | (d) is able to exercise a significant influence over the management of P by virtue of A's shareholding in P; or
-- src:2000 | (e) is entitled to exercise, or control the exercise of, voting power in C which, if it consists of voting rights, constitutes at least 10% of the voting rights in C; or
-- src:2001 | (f) is able to exercise a significant influence over the management of C by virtue of A's entitlement to exercise, or control the exercise of, voting rights in C; or
-- src:2002 | (g) is entitled to exercise, or control the exercise of, voting power in P which, if it consists of voting rights, constitutes at least 10% of the voting rights in P; or
-- src:2003 | (h) is able to exercise a significant influence over the management of P by virtue of A's entitlement to exercise, or control the exercise of, voting rights in P.
@ref Sch 2 para 6(4) (src:1995-2003)
GIVEN holders IS A LIST OF `Holder of an interest in a company`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 6(4) — influence over the management of C or P` holders MEANS
    any (GIVEN holder YIELD IF `Sch 2 para 6(5) — the holder counts as A or one of A's associates` holder THEN ((holder's `able to exercise a significant influence over the management of C by virtue of the holder's shareholding in C`) OR (holder's `able to exercise a significant influence over the management of P by virtue of the holder's shareholding in P`) OR (holder's `able to exercise a significant influence over the management of C by virtue of the holder's entitlement to exercise, or control the exercise of, voting rights in C`) OR (holder's `able to exercise a significant influence over the management of P by virtue of the holder's entitlement to exercise, or control the exercise of, voting rights in P`)) ELSE FALSE) holders

-- Paragraph 6(3) and (4): A has a material interest in C (and so is an "owner" of C) if any of limbs (a) to (h) holds. The 10% figure is the text's.
-- src:1994 | (3) In this paragraph, “owner”, in relation to a company (“C”), means a person (“A”) who has a material interest in C.
-- src:1995 | (4) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (3), A has a material interest in C if A—
-- src:1996 | (a) holds at least 10% of the shares in C; or
-- src:1997 | (b) is able to exercise a significant influence over the management of C by virtue of A's shareholding in C; or
-- src:1998 | (c) holds at least 10% of the shares in a parent undertaking (“P”) of C; or
-- src:1999 | (d) is able to exercise a significant influence over the management of P by virtue of A's shareholding in P; or
-- src:2000 | (e) is entitled to exercise, or control the exercise of, voting power in C which, if it consists of voting rights, constitutes at least 10% of the voting rights in C; or
-- src:2001 | (f) is able to exercise a significant influence over the management of C by virtue of A's entitlement to exercise, or control the exercise of, voting rights in C; or
-- src:2002 | (g) is entitled to exercise, or control the exercise of, voting power in P which, if it consists of voting rights, constitutes at least 10% of the voting rights in P; or
-- src:2003 | (h) is able to exercise a significant influence over the management of P by virtue of A's entitlement to exercise, or control the exercise of, voting rights in P.
@ref Sch 2 para 6(3) and (4) (src:1994-2003)
GIVEN holders IS A LIST OF `Holder of an interest in a company`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 6(4) — A has a material interest in C` holders MEANS
    (`Sch 2 para 6(5)(c) — the percentage of the shares in C held by the person and the associates together` holders AT LEAST 10)
    OR (`Sch 2 para 6(5)(c) — the percentage of the shares in P held by the person and the associates together` holders AT LEAST 10)
    OR (`Sch 2 para 6(5)(c) — the percentage of the voting rights in C held by the person and the associates together` holders AT LEAST 10)
    OR (`Sch 2 para 6(5)(c) — the percentage of the voting rights in P held by the person and the associates together` holders AT LEAST 10)
    OR (`Sch 2 para 6(4) — influence over the management of C or P` holders)

-- A person who may be an owner or director of the company.
-- src:1986 | (1) A claimant is to be treated as not liable to make rent payments where the liability to make them is owed to a company and the owners or directors of the company include—
@ref Sch 2 para 6(1) (src:1986)
DECLARE `Person who may be an owner or director of a company` HAS
    `is a director of the company`                                                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the holdings of the person and the person's associates`                                                      IS A LIST OF `Holder of an interest in a company`

-- src:1986 | (1) A claimant is to be treated as not liable to make rent payments where the liability to make them is owed to a company and the owners or directors of the company include—
@ref Sch 2 para 6(1) and (3) (src:1986) (src:1994)
GIVEN person IS A `Person who may be an owner or director of a company`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 6(1) — the person is an owner or director of the company` person MEANS
    (person's `is a director of the company`)
    OR (`Sch 2 para 6(4) — A has a material interest in C` (person's `the holdings of the person and the person's associates`))

-- Paragraph 6(1): the owners or directors include the claimant, the other member of the couple, a qualifying young person for whom either is
-- responsible, or a close relative of any of those who lives in the accommodation with the claimant.
-- src:1985 | 6 Liability to make rent and other payments to company
-- src:1986 | (1) A claimant is to be treated as not liable to make rent payments where the liability to make them is owed to a company and the owners or directors of the company include—
-- src:1987 | (a) the claimant;
-- src:1988 | (b) if the claimant is a member of a couple, the other member;
-- src:1989 | (c) a qualifying young person for whom a person who falls within paragraph (a) or (b) is responsible; or
-- src:1990 | (d) a close relative of any of the above who lives in the accommodation with the claimant.
@ref Sch 2 para 6(1) (src:1985-1990)
DECLARE `Company to which a liability is owed` HAS
    `the claimant as a possible owner or director`                                                                         IS A `Person who may be an owner or director of a company`
    `the other member of the couple as a possible owner or director`                                                       IS A `Person who may be an owner or director of a company`
    -- out of range: reg 4 (piece uc1), "responsible for a qualifying young person"
    `a qualifying young person for whom the claimant or the other member is responsible, as a possible owner or director`  IS A `Person who may be an owner or director of a company`
    `a close relative of any of the above, as a possible owner or director`                                                IS A `Person who may be an owner or director of a company`
    `the close relative as a possible close relative`                                                                       IS A `Possible close relative`
    `the close relative lives in the accommodation with the claimant`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1986 | (1) A claimant is to be treated as not liable to make rent payments where the liability to make them is owed to a company and the owners or directors of the company include—
-- src:1987 | (a) the claimant;
-- src:1988 | (b) if the claimant is a member of a couple, the other member;
-- src:1989 | (c) a qualifying young person for whom a person who falls within paragraph (a) or (b) is responsible; or
-- src:1990 | (d) a close relative of any of the above who lives in the accommodation with the claimant.
@ref Sch 2 para 6(1) (src:1986-1990)
GIVEN company IS A `Company to which a liability is owed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 6(1) — the owners or directors of the company include a listed person` company MEANS
    (`Sch 2 para 6(1) — the person is an owner or director of the company` (company's `the claimant as a possible owner or director`))
    OR (`Sch 2 para 6(1) — the person is an owner or director of the company` (company's `the other member of the couple as a possible owner or director`))
    OR (`Sch 2 para 6(1) — the person is an owner or director of the company` (company's `a qualifying young person for whom the claimant or the other member is responsible, as a possible owner or director`))
    OR (    (`reg 2 — close relative` (company's `the close relative as a possible close relative`))
        AND (company's `the close relative lives in the accommodation with the claimant`)
        AND (`Sch 2 para 6(1) — the person is an owner or director of the company` (company's `a close relative of any of the above, as a possible owner or director`)))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Part 2, paragraph 7: liability to a trustee of a trust whose trustees or beneficiaries include a listed person.
-- src:2026 | 7 Liability to make rent and other payments to a trust
-- src:2027 | (1) A claimant is to be treated as not liable to make rent payments where the liability to make them is owed to a trustee of a trust and the trustees or beneficiaries of the trust include—
-- src:2028 | (a) the claimant;
-- src:2029 | (b) if the claimant is a member of a couple, the other member;
-- src:2030 | (c) a child or qualifying young person for whom a person who falls within paragraph (a) or (b) is responsible; or
-- src:2031 | (d) a close relative of any of the above who lives in the accommodation with the claimant.
@ref Sch 2 para 7(1) (src:2026-2031)
DECLARE `Trust to which a liability is owed` HAS
    `the liability is owed to a trustee of a trust`                                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trustees or beneficiaries include the claimant`                                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trustees or beneficiaries include the other member of the couple`                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    -- out of range: reg 4 (piece uc1), "responsible for a child or qualifying young person"
    `the trustees or beneficiaries include a child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant or the other member is responsible`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trustees or beneficiaries include a close relative of any of the above who lives in the accommodation with the claimant`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2027 | (1) A claimant is to be treated as not liable to make rent payments where the liability to make them is owed to a trustee of a trust and the trustees or beneficiaries of the trust include—
-- src:2028 | (a) the claimant;
-- src:2029 | (b) if the claimant is a member of a couple, the other member;
-- src:2030 | (c) a child or qualifying young person for whom a person who falls within paragraph (a) or (b) is responsible; or
-- src:2031 | (d) a close relative of any of the above who lives in the accommodation with the claimant.
@ref Sch 2 para 7(1) (src:2027-2031)
GIVEN trust IS A `Trust to which a liability is owed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 7(1) — the trustees or beneficiaries include a listed person` trust MEANS
    (trust's `the liability is owed to a trustee of a trust`)
    AND (    (trust's `the trustees or beneficiaries include the claimant`)
          OR (trust's `the trustees or beneficiaries include the other member of the couple`)
          OR (trust's `the trustees or beneficiaries include a child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant or the other member is responsible`)
          OR (trust's `the trustees or beneficiaries include a close relative of any of the above who lives in the accommodation with the claimant`))

