-- Part 2, paragraph 8: liability to a person who lives in the claimant's household.
-- src:2035 | 8 Liability to make owner-occupier and other payments to member of same household
-- src:2036 | (1) A claimant is to be treated as not liable to make owner-occupier payments where the liability to make the payments is owed to a person who lives in the claimant's household.
-- src:2037 | (2) A claimant who is treated under sub-paragraph (1) as not liable to make owner-occupier payments to any person is also to be treated as not liable to make service charge payments where the liability to make the service charge payments is to the same person.
-- src:2038 | (3) A claimant is to be treated as not liable to make service charge payments where—
-- src:2039 | (a) there is no liability to make rent payments or owner-occupier payments; but
-- src:2040 | (b) the liability to make service charge payments is to a person who lives in the claimant's household.
@ref Sch 2 para 8 (src:2035-2040)
DECLARE `Household creditor` HAS
    `the liability is owed to a person who lives in the claimant's household`                                          IS A BOOLEAN

-- Paragraph 6(2) and 7(2) and 5(2) and 8(2): a service charge liability is also treated as not owed where the claimant is treated as not liable to
-- make rent payments (or, for paragraph 8, owner-occupier payments) and the service charge creditor is within the same test.
-- The facts below are those of the SERVICE CHARGE liability; the three flags say whether the rent (or owner-occupier) payments have been so treated.
-- src:1984 | (2) A claimant who is treated under sub-paragraph (1) as not liable to make rent payments to any person is also to be treated as not liable to make service charge payments where the liability to make the service charge payments is to the same person.
-- src:1991 | (2) A claimant who is treated under sub-paragraph (1) as not liable to make rent payments to the company is also to be treated as not liable to make service charge payments where the liability to make the service charge payments is to—
-- src:1992 | (a) the same company; or
-- src:1993 | (b) another company of which the owners or directors include any of the persons listed in sub-paragraph (1)(a) to (d).
-- src:2032 | (2) A claimant who is treated under sub-paragraph (1) as not liable to make rent payments to the trustee of a trust is also to be treated as not liable to make service charge payments where the liability to make the service charge payments is to—
-- src:2033 | (a) a trustee of the same trust; or
-- src:2034 | (b) a trustee of another trust of which the trustees or beneficiaries include any of the persons listed in sub-paragraph (1)(a) to (d).
-- src:2037 | (2) A claimant who is treated under sub-paragraph (1) as not liable to make owner-occupier payments to any person is also to be treated as not liable to make service charge payments where the liability to make the service charge payments is to the same person.
@ref Sch 2 para 5(2), 6(2), 7(2) and 8(2) (src:1984) (src:1991-1993) (src:2032-2034) (src:2037)
DECLARE `Facts about a liability, as Part 2 reads them` HAS
    `kind of payment`                                                                                                  IS A `Kind of payment under Schedule 2`
    `the creditor as a possible person within paragraph 5`                                                             IS A `Person to whom a liability is owed`
    `the creditor as a possible company`                                                                               IS A `Company to which a liability is owed`
    `the creditor as a possible trust`                                                                                 IS A `Trust to which a liability is owed`
    `the creditor as a possible household member`                                                                      IS A `Household creditor`
    `the claimant is treated under paragraph 5(1) as not liable to make rent payments to that person`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant is treated under paragraph 6(1) as not liable to make rent payments to a company`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant is treated under paragraph 7(1) as not liable to make rent payments to a trustee of a trust`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant is treated under paragraph 8(1) as not liable to make owner-occupier payments to that person`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is no liability to make rent payments or owner-occupier payments`                                            IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1974 | 5 Liability to make rent and other payments to close relative
-- src:1975 | (1) A claimant is to be treated as not liable to make rent payments where the liability to make them is owed to a person who lives in the accommodation and who is—
-- src:1976 | (a) if the claimant is a member of a couple, the other member; or
-- src:1977 | (b) a child or qualifying young person for whom—
-- src:1978 | (i) the claimant is responsible, or
-- src:1979 | (ii) if the claimant is a member of a couple, the other member is responsible; or
-- src:1980 | (c) a close relative of—
-- src:1981 | (i) the claimant, or
-- src:1982 | (ii) if the claimant is a member of a couple, the other member, or
-- src:1983 | (iii) any child or qualifying young person who falls within paragraph (b).
-- src:1984 | (2) A claimant who is treated under sub-paragraph (1) as not liable to make rent payments to any person is also to be treated as not liable to make service charge payments where the liability to make the service charge payments is to the same person.
@ref Sch 2 para 5 (src:1974-1984)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about a liability, as Part 2 reads them`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 5 — the claimant is treated as not liable (close relative)` facts MEANS
    (`Sch 2 para 5(1) — the liability is owed to a person who lives in the accommodation and is within paragraph 5(1)(a) to (c)` (facts's `the creditor as a possible person within paragraph 5`))
    AND (    ((facts's `kind of payment`) EQUALS `rent payments`)
          OR (    ((facts's `kind of payment`) EQUALS `service charge payments`)
              AND (facts's `the claimant is treated under paragraph 5(1) as not liable to make rent payments to that person`)))

