    OR (`Sch 2 para 8 — the claimant is treated as not liable (household)` facts)

-- Part 2, paragraph 9: no liability for any amount that is an increase in the sum otherwise payable, resulting from arrears. Paragraph 9(2):
-- it does not apply if the claimant is treated as not liable under paragraphs 5 to 8 (the whole payment is then already outside the claimant's liability).
-- src:2041 | 9 Arrears of payments
-- src:2042 | (1) A claimant is to be treated as not liable to make payments in respect of any amount which—
-- src:2043 | (a) represents an increase in the sum that would be otherwise payable; and
-- src:2044 | (b) is the result of—
-- src:2045 | (i) outstanding arrears of any payment or charge in respect of the accommodation,
-- src:2046 | (ii) outstanding arrears of any payment or charge in respect of other accommodation, previously occupied by the claimant, or
-- src:2047 | (iii) any other unpaid liability to make a payment or charge.
-- src:2048 | (2) Sub-paragraph (1) does not apply if the claimant is treated as not liable to make the payments under any of the preceding provisions of this Part of this Schedule.
@ref Sch 2 para 9 (src:2041-2048)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about a liability, as Part 2 reads them`
      `amount that represents an increase in the sum otherwise payable and results from arrears or any other unpaid liability` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 2 para 9 — the amount for which the claimant is treated as not liable because of arrears` facts `amount that represents an increase in the sum otherwise payable and results from arrears or any other unpaid liability` MEANS
    IF `Sch 2 paras 5 to 8 — the claimant is treated as not liable to make the payments` facts
    THEN 0
    ELSE `amount that represents an increase in the sum otherwise payable and results from arrears or any other unpaid liability`

-- Part 2, paragraph 10: contrived liability. The Secretary of State's satisfaction is a stated input.
-- src:2049 | 10 Contrived liability
-- src:2050 | (1) A claimant is to be treated as not liable to make payments where the Secretary of State is satisfied that the liability to make the payments was contrived in order to secure the inclusion of the housing costs element in an award of universal credit or to increase the amount of that element.
-- src:2051 | (2) Sub-paragraph (1) does not apply if the claimant is treated as not liable to make the payments under any of the preceding provisions of this Part of this Schedule.
@ref Sch 2 para 10 (src:2049-2051)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about a liability, as Part 2 reads them`
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the liability to make the payments was contrived in order to secure the inclusion of the housing costs element in an award of universal credit or to increase the amount of that element` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 10 — the claimant is treated as not liable because the liability was contrived` facts `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the liability to make the payments was contrived in order to secure the inclusion of the housing costs element in an award of universal credit or to increase the amount of that element` MEANS
    (NOT (`Sch 2 paras 5 to 8 — the claimant is treated as not liable to make the payments` facts))
    AND `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the liability to make the payments was contrived in order to secure the inclusion of the housing costs element in an award of universal credit or to increase the amount of that element`

