-- The composite answer, over a whole payment: liable in fact, or treated as liable under Part 1, and not treated as not liable under Part 2
-- (paragraphs 5 to 8 and paragraph 10; paragraph 9 reduces the amount rather than the liability and is read by its own rule).
-- src:1953 | 1 Certain other persons liable to make payments
-- src:1974 | 5 Liability to make rent and other payments to close relative
@ref Sch 2 paras 1 to 10 (src:1953) (src:1974)
DECLARE `Part 1 facts about a liability` HAS
    `the claimant is liable in fact`                                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person who is liable`                                                                          IS A `Person who is liable to make the payments`
    `claim basis`                                                                                       IS A `Claim basis`
    `claiming as a single person by virtue of regulation 3(4)`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `failure to pay`                                                                                    IS A `Failure to pay by the person who is liable`
    `waiver`                                                                                            IS A `Waiver of liability for repair work`
    `the arrangements provide for rent free periods`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the period`                                                                                        IS A `Period of the arrangements`

-- src:1953 | 1 Certain other persons liable to make payments
-- src:1954 | (1) A claimant is to be treated as liable to make payments where the person who is liable to make the payments is—
-- src:1955 | (a) any child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant (or if the claimant is a member of a couple, either member) is responsible; or
-- src:1956 | (b) in the case of a claimant who is a member of a couple claiming as a single person, the other member of the couple.
-- src:1957 | (2) Sub-paragraph (1)(b) does not apply to a person who is claiming as a single person by virtue of regulation 3(4).
-- src:1958 | 2 Failure to pay by the person who is liable
-- src:1959 | (1) A claimant is to be treated as liable to make payments where all of the conditions specified in sub-paragraph (2) are met.
-- src:1960 | (2) These are the conditions—
-- src:1961 | (a) the person who is liable to make the payments is not doing so;
-- src:1962 | (b) the claimant has to make the payments in order to continue occupation of the accommodation;
-- src:1963 | (c) the claimant's circumstances are such that it would be unreasonable to expect them to make other arrangements;
-- src:1964 | (d) it is otherwise reasonable in all the circumstances to treat the claimant as liable to make the payments.
-- src:1965 | (3) In determining what is reasonable for the purposes of sub-paragraph (2)(d) in the case of owner-occupier payments, regard may be had to the fact that continuing to make the payments may benefit the person with the liability to make the payments.
-- src:1966 | 3 Payments waived in return for repair work
-- src:1967 | A claimant is to be treated as liable to make payments where—
-- src:1968 | (a) the liability to make payments is waived by the person (“P”) to whom the liability is owed; and
-- src:1969 | (b) the waiver of that liability is by way of reasonable compensation for reasonable repair or re-decoration works carried out by the claimant to the accommodation which P would otherwise have carried out or been required to carry out.
-- src:1970 | 4 Rent free periods
-- src:1971 | (1) Where the arrangements under which the claimant occupies the accommodation provide for rent free periods, the claimant is to be treated as liable to make rent payments and service charge payments in respect of accommodation for the whole of any rent free period.
-- src:1972 | (2) In paragraph (1), “rent free period” has the meaning given in paragraph 7(4) of Schedule 4.
@ref Sch 2 Part 1 (src:1953-1972)
GIVEN part1 IS A `Part 1 facts about a liability`
      kind IS A `Kind of payment under Schedule 2`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 Part 1 — the claimant is treated as liable under paragraphs 1 to 4` part1 kind MEANS
    (`Sch 2 para 1 — the claimant is treated as liable because of the person who is liable` (part1's `the person who is liable`) (part1's `claim basis`) (part1's `claiming as a single person by virtue of regulation 3(4)`))
    OR (`Sch 2 para 2 — the claimant is treated as liable because the person who is liable has failed to pay` (part1's `failure to pay`))
    OR (`Sch 2 para 3 — the claimant is treated as liable although the liability is waived for repair work` (part1's waiver))
    OR (`Sch 2 para 4 — the claimant is treated as liable for the whole of a rent free period` kind (part1's `the arrangements provide for rent free periods`) (part1's `the period`))

-- src:1953 | 1 Certain other persons liable to make payments
-- src:1954 | (1) A claimant is to be treated as liable to make payments where the person who is liable to make the payments is—
-- src:1955 | (a) any child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant (or if the claimant is a member of a couple, either member) is responsible; or
-- src:1956 | (b) in the case of a claimant who is a member of a couple claiming as a single person, the other member of the couple.
-- src:1957 | (2) Sub-paragraph (1)(b) does not apply to a person who is claiming as a single person by virtue of regulation 3(4).
-- src:1958 | 2 Failure to pay by the person who is liable
-- src:1959 | (1) A claimant is to be treated as liable to make payments where all of the conditions specified in sub-paragraph (2) are met.
-- src:1960 | (2) These are the conditions—
-- src:1961 | (a) the person who is liable to make the payments is not doing so;
-- src:1962 | (b) the claimant has to make the payments in order to continue occupation of the accommodation;
-- src:1963 | (c) the claimant's circumstances are such that it would be unreasonable to expect them to make other arrangements;
-- src:1964 | (d) it is otherwise reasonable in all the circumstances to treat the claimant as liable to make the payments.
-- src:1965 | (3) In determining what is reasonable for the purposes of sub-paragraph (2)(d) in the case of owner-occupier payments, regard may be had to the fact that continuing to make the payments may benefit the person with the liability to make the payments.
-- src:1966 | 3 Payments waived in return for repair work
-- src:1967 | A claimant is to be treated as liable to make payments where—
-- src:1968 | (a) the liability to make payments is waived by the person (“P”) to whom the liability is owed; and
-- src:1969 | (b) the waiver of that liability is by way of reasonable compensation for reasonable repair or re-decoration works carried out by the claimant to the accommodation which P would otherwise have carried out or been required to carry out.
-- src:1970 | 4 Rent free periods
-- src:1971 | (1) Where the arrangements under which the claimant occupies the accommodation provide for rent free periods, the claimant is to be treated as liable to make rent payments and service charge payments in respect of accommodation for the whole of any rent free period.
-- src:1972 | (2) In paragraph (1), “rent free period” has the meaning given in paragraph 7(4) of Schedule 4.
@ref Sch 2 Part 1 (src:1953-1972)
GIVEN part1 IS A `Part 1 facts about a liability`
      kind IS A `Kind of payment under Schedule 2`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 — the claimant is liable in fact or treated as liable under Part 1` part1 kind MEANS
    (part1's `the claimant is liable in fact`)
    OR (`Sch 2 Part 1 — the claimant is treated as liable under paragraphs 1 to 4` part1 kind)

-- src:1952 | PART 1 — Treated as liable to make payments
-- src:1953 | 1 Certain other persons liable to make payments
-- src:1973 | PART 2 — Treated as not liable to make payments
-- src:1974 | 5 Liability to make rent and other payments to close relative
@ref Sch 2 Parts 1 and 2 (src:1952-1953) (src:1973-1974)
GIVEN part1 IS A `Part 1 facts about a liability`
      facts IS A `Facts about a liability, as Part 2 reads them`
      contrived IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 — the claimant is liable to make the payments` part1 facts contrived MEANS
    (`Sch 2 — the claimant is liable in fact or treated as liable under Part 1` part1 (facts's `kind of payment`))
    AND (NOT (`Sch 2 paras 5 to 8 — the claimant is treated as not liable to make the payments` facts))
    AND (NOT contrived)
